      longDescription: "Hand Tracking follows hands on a live webcam feed. MediaPipe Hands finds each hand anywhere in the frame and returns 21 landmarks, from the wrist to each fingertip, which the script draws as a skeleton over the image.\n\nFrom those landmarks it builds a box around the hand: the outer edges of the five fingers, the wrist as the bottom, and a margin on every side. The box is then squared by padding its shorter side, so the hand keeps its proportions, and it is drawn only when it sits fully inside the frame. A square, centered crop is exactly what an image classifier expects as input.\n\nI wrote it in February 2022, the same month as my sign-language app, which needed the hand inside a fixed box on screen. This takes the opposite approach: find the hand wherever it is, with no training data of my own.",
